    "markdown": {
      "es": "# Excrypt commands\n\nFuente: [Excrypt commands](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/Welcome)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:12:31.053Z\n\n---\n\n7.6.1.x\n\n# Excrypt commands\n\nFuturex's native command format. The broadest feature coverage; new functionality lands here first.\n\nCurrent release\n\nv7.6.1.39[Release notes→](https://docs.futurex.com/Excrypt_HSM/7.6.1.x/release-notes/firmware-release/76139)\n\n<a id=\"quickstart-heading\"></a>\n\n## Quickstart\n\nOpen a TCP session using netcat, telnet, or puTTY and send your first Excrypt command (`ECHO`) to verify the HSM is reachable. Replace `HSM_HOST` with your appliance IP or hostname.\n\n```\nnc HSM_HOST 9000\n\n[AOECHO;]\n\n# Response: [AOECHO;BC7.6.1.34ck;]\n```\n\n> **Note:** Response fields are token-prefixed and separated by semicolons: `AOECHO` is the command ID, `BC` returns the firmware version.\n> \n> \n> \n> Excrypt and Standard commands share the **Production port**: **9000** for clear TCP, **9100** for TLS.\n\n<a id=\"browse-heading\"></a>\n\n## Browse the commands\n\nFind the section you need by what you're working on. Each section lists every command with a one-line description.\n\n### Keys\n\nGenerate, derive, translate, wrap, and import keys.\n\n- [Keys overview](keys/Overview.md)\n- [Generate keys](keys/Overview.md#generate)\n- [Translate keys](keys/Overview.md#translate)\n\n### Data encryption\n\nSymmetric, format-preserving, point-to-point, tokenization.\n\n- [Data encryption overview](data_encryption/Overview.md)\n- [Symmetric encryption](data_encryption/Overview.md#symmetric)\n- [Point-to-point encryption](data_encryption/Overview.md#point-to-point)\n\n### PINs\n\nTranslate, verify, and generate PIN blocks and offsets.\n\n- [PINs overview](pins/Overview.md)\n- [Translate PIN blocks](pins/Overview.md#translate)\n- [Verify PINs](pins/Overview.md#verify)\n\n### Payments and cards\n\nEMV, card verification, mobile pay (Apple Pay, Google Pay, HCE).\n\n- [Payments and cards overview](payments_cards/Overview.md)\n- [EMV cryptograms](payments_cards/Overview.md#emv)\n- [Mobile pay tokens](payments_cards/Overview.md#mobile-pay)\n\n### Signatures and MACs\n\nSign and verify with HMAC, CMAC, RSA, and ECDSA.\n\n- [Signatures and MACs overview](signatures_macs/Overview.md)\n- [Generate MACs](signatures_macs/Overview.md#generate)\n- [Verify signatures](signatures_macs/Overview.md#verify)\n\n### Asymmetric cryptography\n\nRSA or ECC encrypt/decrypt and DH key agreement.\n\n- [Asymmetric cryptography overview](asymmetric/Overview.md)\n- [Encrypt or decrypt](asymmetric/Overview.md#encrypt-or-decrypt)\n- [Derive shared secret](asymmetric/Overview.md#derive-shared-secret)\n\n### Certificates\n\nGenerate, request, verify, and inspect certificates and CRLs.\n\n- [Certificates overview](certificates/Overview.md)\n- [Generate certificates](certificates/Overview.md#generate)\n- [Verify certificates](certificates/Overview.md#verify)\n\n### System\n\nAdministration, authentication, TLS, utilities.\n\n- [System overview](system/Overview.md)\n- [Administration](system/Overview.md#admin)\n- [Utilities](system/Overview.md#utility)\n\n### Index\n\nFull alphabetical index of Excrypt commands.\n\n- [Command index](command-index.md)\n",
      "en": "# Excrypt commands\n\nFuente: [Excrypt commands](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/Welcome)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:12:31.053Z\n\n---\n\n7.6.1.x\n\n# Excrypt commands\n\nFuturex's native command format. The broadest feature coverage; new functionality lands here first.\n\nCurrent release\n\nv7.6.1.39[Release notes→](https://docs.futurex.com/Excrypt_HSM/7.6.1.x/release-notes/firmware-release/76139)\n\n<a id=\"quickstart-heading\"></a>\n\n## Quickstart\n\nOpen a TCP session using netcat, telnet, or puTTY and send your first Excrypt command (`ECHO`) to verify the HSM is reachable. Replace `HSM_HOST` with your appliance IP or hostname.\n\n```\nnc HSM_HOST 9000\n\n[AOECHO;]\n\n# Response: [AOECHO;BC7.6.1.34ck;]\n```\n\n> **Note:** Response fields are token-prefixed and separated by semicolons: `AOECHO` is the command ID, `BC` returns the firmware version.\n> \n> \n> \n> Excrypt and Standard commands share the **Production port**: **9000** for clear TCP, **9100** for TLS.\n\n<a id=\"browse-heading\"></a>\n\n## Browse the commands\n\nFind the section you need by what you're working on. Each section lists every command with a one-line description.\n\n### Keys\n\nGenerate, derive, translate, wrap, and import keys.\n\n- [Keys overview](keys/Overview.md)\n- [Generate keys](keys/Overview.md#generate)\n- [Translate keys](keys/Overview.md#translate)\n\n### Data encryption\n\nSymmetric, format-preserving, point-to-point, tokenization.\n\n- [Data encryption overview](data_encryption/Overview.md)\n- [Symmetric encryption](data_encryption/Overview.md#symmetric)\n- [Point-to-point encryption](data_encryption/Overview.md#point-to-point)\n\n### PINs\n\nTranslate, verify, and generate PIN blocks and offsets.\n\n- [PINs overview](pins/Overview.md)\n- [Translate PIN blocks](pins/Overview.md#translate)\n- [Verify PINs](pins/Overview.md#verify)\n\n### Payments and cards\n\nEMV, card verification, mobile pay (Apple Pay, Google Pay, HCE).\n\n- [Payments and cards overview](payments_cards/Overview.md)\n- [EMV cryptograms](payments_cards/Overview.md#emv)\n- [Mobile pay tokens](payments_cards/Overview.md#mobile-pay)\n\n### Signatures and MACs\n\nSign and verify with HMAC, CMAC, RSA, and ECDSA.\n\n- [Signatures and MACs overview](signatures_macs/Overview.md)\n- [Generate MACs](signatures_macs/Overview.md#generate)\n- [Verify signatures](signatures_macs/Overview.md#verify)\n\n### Asymmetric cryptography\n\nRSA or ECC encrypt/decrypt and DH key agreement.\n\n- [Asymmetric cryptography overview](asymmetric/Overview.md)\n- [Encrypt or decrypt](asymmetric/Overview.md#encrypt-or-decrypt)\n- [Derive shared secret](asymmetric/Overview.md#derive-shared-secret)\n\n### Certificates\n\nGenerate, request, verify, and inspect certificates and CRLs.\n\n- [Certificates overview](certificates/Overview.md)\n- [Generate certificates](certificates/Overview.md#generate)\n- [Verify certificates](certificates/Overview.md#verify)\n\n### System\n\nAdministration, authentication, TLS, utilities.\n\n- [System overview](system/Overview.md)\n- [Administration](system/Overview.md#admin)\n- [Utilities](system/Overview.md#utility)\n\n### Index\n\nFull alphabetical index of Excrypt commands.\n\n- [Command index](command-index.md)\n"
    }
